{
  peppy_schema: "contract/v1",
  manifest: {
    name: "limb_state",
    tag: "v1",
    description: [
      "The measured state of every limb of a multi-arm manipulator, as one whole-robot snapshot per message: joint positions, the gripper grasp-point pose of each arm, and each gripper's opening.",
      "Names match limb_motion addressing: the same arm and gripper names select limbs there and label them here, and get_limb_names answers them on demand, so a consumer can address a limb and size the arrays before a snapshot arrives. Distinct from the streamed per-pair states on the joint_link / gripper_link / pose_link pairings: this is a robot-wide summary any consumer can read without holding a pairing.",
      "Slicing rule for the per-arm arrays, all index-aligned with arm_names:",
      "joint_positions concatenates each arm's joints in arm_names order; arm i's vector starts at the sum of joints_per_arm[0..i] and runs joints_per_arm[i] entries.",
      "grasp_points holds one grasp-point pose per arm, in arm_names order.",
      "Gripper arrays are index-aligned with gripper_names, independent of the arm arrays.",
      "A grasp-point pose is the gripper's grasp point in the robot frame, which each limb_states names in frame, at the snapshot's timestamp. On a gripper whose jaws close symmetrically, it is on the jaw closing axis midway between the pads. The SO-101 gripper has one moving jaw, so the midpoint of its pads moves with the opening. Thus, the SO-101 reports a fixed point near its jaws.",
      "The robot frame is the robot frame of transforms: the root link of the robot's URDF. The implementer publishes on transforms, at the timestamp of each limb_states, the transform of each arm joint from that snapshot's joint_positions and the transforms of each gripper's joints measured at that timestamp, so each arm's grasp-point pose equals the place of the arm's grasp link, the last link of its chain in the SRDF, in the robot frame at that timestamp, within 1e-9 m and rad.",
    ],
  },
  interfaces: {
    topics: [
      {
        name: "limb_states",
        description: "One snapshot of the measured state of every limb of the robot: the joints and the grasp-point pose of each arm, and the opening of each gripper, captured at timestamp.",
        // High-frequency stream where only the latest snapshot matters;
        // occasional drops are acceptable.
        qos_profile: "sensor_data",
        message_format: {
          frame: { $type: "string", $description: "The frame of the record's values, as transforms names frames." },
          timestamp: { $type: "time", $description: "The time on the clock of transforms at which the values hold." },
          arm_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The implementer's fixed set of arm names (e.g. \"left_arm\"), in its fixed order." },
          joints_per_arm: { $type: "array", $items: "u32", $description: "Joint count of each arm, index-aligned with arm_names." },
          joint_positions: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Measured joint positions (rad for revolute joints, m for prismatic), each arm's vector concatenated in arm_names order per the slicing rule of this contract." },
          grasp_points: {
            $type: "array",
            $description: "The measured grasp-point pose of each arm, in the robot frame, frame, at timestamp, in arm_names order.",
            $items: {
              $type: "object",
              position: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 3, $description: "x, y, z (m)." },
              orientation: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $length: 4, $description: "A unit quaternion [x, y, z, w]." },
            },
          },
          gripper_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The implementer's fixed set of gripper names (e.g. \"left_gripper\"), in its fixed order." },
          gripper_openings: { $type: "array", $items: "f64", $description: "Measured opening fraction of each gripper (0 = closed, 1 = fully open), index-aligned with gripper_names." },
        },
      },
    ],
    services: [
      {
        name: "get_limb_names",
        description: "Give the robot's limb names and the joints behind each arm name: the names limb_motion goals address and limb_states labels, held by the implementer whatever its limbs are measuring.",
        response_message_format: {
          arm_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The implementer's fixed set of arm names (e.g. \"left_arm\"), in its fixed order." },
          joints_per_arm: { $type: "array", $items: "u32", $description: "Joint count of each arm, index-aligned with arm_names." },
          gripper_names: { $type: "array", $items: "string", $description: "The implementer's fixed set of gripper names (e.g. \"left_gripper\"), in its fixed order." },
        },
      },
    ],
  },
}
